          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong Wess-Zumino-Witten model
            (or
            %strong WZW model
            for short, also called
            %strong Wess-Zumino-Novikov-Witten
            model, or short
            %strong WZNW
            model) is a 2-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            whose target space is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
          %p
            This may be regarded as the boundary theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            for Lie group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            The
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+operator+algebra"} vertex operator algebra
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/current+algebra"} current algebra
          %h2#ActionFunctional Action functional
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
            of the WZW over a 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"}> dimension
            al
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is the space of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : \Sigma \to G
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            of the WZW
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            is the sum of two terms, a kinetic term and a topological term
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi WZW
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi kin
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi top
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_{WZW} = S_{kin} + S_{top}
                  \\,.
          %h3#KineticTerm Kinetic term
          %p
            The Lie group canonically carries a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            and the kinetic term is the standard one for
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
          %h3#TopologicalTerm Topological term – WZW term
          %h4#WZWTermFor2dModel For the 2d WZW model
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+n-form"} differential (p+2)-form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
