                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %h3#DBranes D-branes for the WZW model
          %p
            The characterization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open string
            WZW model on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            comes from two consistency conditions:
          %ol
            %li
              %p geometrical condition:
              %p
                For the open string
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CFT"} CFT
                to still have
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/current+algebra"} current algebra
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
                symmetry, hence for half the current algebra symmetry of the closed WZW string to be preserved, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
                need to be
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
                of the group manifold (see e.g.
                %a{:href => "#AlekseevSchomerus"} Alekseev-Schomerus
                for a brief review and further pointers). These conjugacy classes are therefore also called the
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong symmetric D-branes
              %p
                Notice that these conjugacy classes are equivalently the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leaves"} leaves
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation"} foliation
                induced by the canonical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan-Dirac+structure"} Cartan-Dirac structure
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+structure"} Dirac structure
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+dg-submanifold"} Lagrangian sub-Lie 2-algebroids
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+Lie+2-algebroid"} Courant Lie 2-algebroid
                which is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+groupoid"} higher gauge groupoid
                (see there) of the background
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
                on
                = succeed ".(It" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
                that such a foliation be thought of as a higher real
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
            %li
              %p cohomological condition:
              %p
                In order for the Kapustin-part of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten-Kapustin+anomaly"} Freed-Witten-Kapustin anomaly
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
                of the open WZW string to vanish, the D-brane must be equipped with a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton gauge field
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+unitary+bundle"} twisted unitary bundle
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe+module"}> bundle gerbe module
                ) of some rank
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                for the restriction of the ambient
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
                to the brane.
              %p
                For
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
                Lie groups only the rank-1 Chan-Paton gauge fields and their direct sums play a role, and their existence corresponds to a trivialization of the underlying
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"}> bundle gerbe
                ) of the restriction of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
                to the brane. There is then a discrete finite collection of symmetric D-branes =
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
                satisfying this condition, and these are called the
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong integral symmetric D-branes
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#AlekseevSchomerus"} Alekseev-Schomerus
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#GW"} Gawedzki-Reis
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#AlekseevSchomerus"} Alekseev-Schomerus
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bohr-Sommerfeld+leaf"} Bohr-Sommerfeld leaf
              %p
                More generally, on non-simply connected group manifolds there are nontrivial higher rank
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+unitary+bundles"} twisted unitary bundles
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+fields"} Chan-Paton gauge fields
                over conjugacy classes and hence the cohomological “integrality” or “Bohr-Sommerfeld”-condition imposed on symmetric D-branes becomes more refined (
                %a{:href => "#Gawedzki04"}> Gawedzki 04
                ).
          %p
            In summary, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            in a Lie group which induce an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open string
            WZW model that a) has one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/current+algebra"} current algebra
            symmetry and b) is
            = succeed "-free" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten-Kapustin+anomaly"} Kapustin-anomaly
            = succeed "-submanifolds" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+class"} conjugacy class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+unitary+bundle"} twisted unitary bundle
            for the restriction of the background
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            to the conjugacy class.
          %h3#quantization Quantization
          %p
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of the WZW model, see at
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+loop+groups"}> quantization of loop groups
                ,
            %li
              %p
