                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gepner+model"} Gepner model
          %h2#References References
          %h3#IntroductionsAndSurveys Introduction and survey
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Goddard"}> Peter Goddard
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Olive"} David Olive
              = succeed "," do
                %em Kac-Moody and Virasoro algebras in relation to quantum physics
              %strong 01
              02 (1986) 303-414 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217751X86000149"}> doi:10.1142/S0217751X86000149
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/18583"} spire:18583
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philippe+Di+Francesco"}> Philippe Di Francesco
                , Pierre Mathieu, David Sénéchal, Part C of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal field theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-2256-9"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4612-2256-9
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bojko+Bakalov"}> Bojko Bakalov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Kirillov"} Alexander Kirillov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Wess-Zumino-Witten model
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on tensor categories and modular functors
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 21
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BakalovKirillov-WZWModel-Ch7OfTensorCat.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~kirillov/tensor/tensor.html"} web
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=ULECT/21"} ams:ulect/21
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Blumenhagen"}> Ralph Blumenhagen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+Plauschinn"} Erik Plauschinn
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to Conformal Field Theory – With Applications to String Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 779
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-00450-6"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-00450-6
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patrick+Meessen"}> Patrick Meessen
                ,
                %em Strings Moving on Group Manifolds: The WZW Model
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.unioviedo.es/hepth/people/Patrick/fysica/zooi/WZW_ClassMunoz.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Meessen-WZWModel.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorenz+Eberhardt"}> Lorenz Eberhardt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Wess-Zumino-Witten models
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://conf.itp.phys.ethz.ch/esi-school/"} YRISW 2019: A modern primer for 2D CFT
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://conf.itp.phys.ethz.ch/esi-school/Lecture_notes/WZW%20models.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Eberhardt-WZWModels.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A basic introduction also to the super-WZW model (and with an eye towards the corresponding
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spectral+triple"} 2-spectral triple
          %ul
            %li#FroehlichGawedzki93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrg+Fr%C3%B6hlich"}> Jürg Fröhlich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gawedzki"} Krzysztof Gawedzki
              = succeed "," do
                %em Conformal Field Theory and Geometry of Strings
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9310187"} arXiv:hep-th/9310187
          %p
            A useful account of the WZW model that encompasses both its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            quantization as well as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/current+algebra"} current algebra
            aspects of the QFT is in
          %ul
            %li#Gawedzki99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gaw%C4%99dzki"}> Krzysztof Gawędzki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Conformal field theory: a case study
              = succeed "," do
                %em Conformal Field Theory – New Non-perturbative Methods In String And Field Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9904145"} arXiv:hep-th/9904145
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429502873"} doi:10.1201/9780429502873
          %p
            This starts in section 2 as a warmup with describing the 1d QFT of a particle propagating on a group manifold. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/states"} states
            is expressed in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} Lie theory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %p
            In section 4 the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of the 2d WZW model is discussed in analogy to that. In lack of a full formalization of the quantization procedure, the author uses the loop algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝓁
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{l} \mathfrak{g}
            – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+Lie+algebra"} affine Lie algebra
            – of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            as the evident analog that replaces
