                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gawedzki"} Krzysztof Gawedzki
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Spectra of Wess-Zumino-Witten models with arbitrary simple groups
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gawedzki"}> Krzysztof Gawedzki
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Topological actions in two-dimensional quantum field theories
          %p
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface+holonomy"} surface holonomy
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundle with connection
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            and at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten+anomaly+cancellation"} Freed-Witten anomaly cancellation
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#DeligneFreed99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"} Daniel Freed
                %em Classical field theory
                (1999) (
                %a{:href => "https://publications.ias.edu/sites/default/files/79_ClassicalFieldTheory.pdf"}> pdf
                )
              %p this is a chapter in
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> P. Deligne
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Etingof"} P. Etingof
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} D.S. Freed
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Kazhdan"} D. Kazhdan
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} E. Witten
                (eds.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"}> Quantum Fields and Strings
                    , A course for mathematicians
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/qft"} web version
          %p
            For the fully general understanding as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface+holonomy"} surface holonomy
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundle with connection
            see the references
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesRelationToGerbesAndCS"} below
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On holomorphic factorization of WZW and coset models
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104249222"} Euclid
          %h3#ReferencesRelationToGerbesAndCS Relation to gerbes and Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundles with connection
            (expressed in terms of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+term"}> WZW term
            ) in this language (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basic+bundle+gerbe"} basic bundle gerbe
          %ul
            %li#GW
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gaw%C4%99dzki"}> Krzysztof Gawędzki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nuno+Reis"} Nuno Reis
                = succeed "," do
                  %em WZW branes and gerbes
                %strong 14
                (2002) 1281-1334 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0205233"}> arXiv:hep-th/0205233
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X02001557"} doi:10.1142/S0129055X02001557
            %li#SchweigertWaldorf07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"}> Christoph Schweigert
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gerbes and Lie Groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Trends and Developments in Lie Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0710.5467"} arXiv:0710.5467
          %p
            Discussion of how this 2-bundle arises from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Carey"}> Alan Carey
              , Stuart Johnson,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Murray"} Michael Murray
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bai-Ling+Wang"} Bai-Ling Wang
              %em Bundle gerbes for Chern-Simons and Wess-Zumino-Witten theories
              Commun.Math.Phys. 259 (2005) 577-613 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0410013"}> arXiv:math/0410013
              )
          %p and related discussion is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"}> Konrad Waldorf
              ,
              %em Multiplicative Bundle Gerbes with Connection
              , Differential Geom. Appl. 28(3), 313-340 (2010) (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0804.4835"}> arXiv:0804.4835
              )
          %p See also Section 2.3.18 and section 4.7 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              (
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/Erlangen2011Schreiber.pdf"}> pdf slides
              ).
          %h3#partition_functions Partition functions
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+functions"} partition functions
            of WZW models:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Terry+Gannon"}> Terry Gannon
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Partition Functions for Heterotic WZW Conformal Field Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9209042"} arXiv:hep-th/9209042
            %li
              %p
                Sameer Murthy,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                %em Localization of strings on group manifolds
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.20028"}> arXiv:2506.20028
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesDBranes D-branes for the WZW model
          %p
            A characterization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            in the WZW model as those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
            that in addition satisfy an integrality (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bohr-Sommerfeld+quantization"}> Bohr-Sommerfeld
            \-type) condition missed in other parts of the literature is stated in
          %ul
            %li#AlekseevSchomerus
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Alekseev"}> Anton Alekseev
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volker+Schomerus"} Volker Schomerus
              = succeed "," do
                %em D-branes in the WZW model
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9812193v2"} arXiv:hep-th/9812193v2
          %p
            The refined interpretation of the integrality condition as a choice of trivialization of the underling
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            over the brane was then noticed in section 7 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gawedzki"}> Krzysztof Gawedzki
              , Nuno Reis,
              = succeed "," do
                %em WZW branes and gerbes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0205233"} arXiv:hep-th/0205233
          %p
            The observation that this is just the special rank-1 case of the more general structure provided by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+unitary+bundle"} twisted unitary bundle
            of some rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            on the D-brane (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe+module"}> gerbe module
            ) which is twisted by the restriction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            to the D-brane – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton gauge field
            – is due to
          %ul
            %li#Gawedzki04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gawedzki"}> Krzysztof Gawedzki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Abelian and non-Abelian branes in WZW models and gerbes
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0406072"} arXiv:hep-th/0406072
          %p
            The observation that the “multiplicative” structure of the WZW-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            (induced from it being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-connection
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verlinde+ring"} Verlinde ring
            fusion product structure on symmetric D-branes equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+fields"} Chan-Paton gauge fields
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Carey"}> Alan Carey
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bai-Ling+Wang"} Bai-Ling Wang
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Fusion of symmetric
                  = succeed "-branes" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0505040"} arXiv:math-ph/0505040
          %p
            The image in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            of these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+fields"} Chan-Paton gauge fields
            over conjugacy classes is shown to generate the
            = succeed "/the" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verlinde+ring"} Verlinde ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+energy+representations"} positive energy representations
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group"} loop group
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckhard+Meinrenken"}> Eckhard Meinrenken
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the quantization of conjugacy classes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0707.3963"} arXiv:0707.3963
          %p
            Formalization of WZW terms in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive homotopy theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#dcct
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %h3#relation_to_dimensional_reduction_of_chernsimons Relation to dimensional reduction of Chern-Simons
          %p
            One can also obtain the WZW-model by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-reduction"} KK-reduction
            from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
          %p E.g.
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Blau"}> Matthias Blau
              , G. Thompson,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Derivation of the Verlinde Formula from Chern-Simons Theory and the G/G model
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9305010"} arXiv:hep-th/9305010
          %p
            A discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Extended+higher+cup-product+Chern-Simons+theories"} Extended higher cup-product Chern-Simons theories
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/A+higher+stacky+perspective+on+Chern-Simons+theory"} A higher stacky perspective on Chern-Simons theory
          %h3#relation_to_extended_tqft Relation to extended TQFT
          %p
            Relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"} extended TQFT
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"}> Dan Freed
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-3-2+8-7-6"} 4-3-2 8-7-6
          %p
            For a formulation of the WZW term in the presence of D-branes as an open-closed smooth
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+field+theory"} functorial field theory
          %ul
            %li#BunkWaldorf21a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Severin+Bunk"}> Severin Bunk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Transgression of D-branes
                %strong 25
                5 (2021) 1095-1198 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/arXiv:1808.04894"}> arXiv:1808.04894
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/ATMP.2021.v25.n5.a1"} doi:10.4310/ATMP.2021.v25.n5.a1
            %li#BunkWaldorf21b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Severin+Bunk"}> Severin Bunk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Smooth functorial field theories from B-fields and D-branes
                %strong 16
                1 (2021) 75-153 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s40062-020-00272-2"}> doi:10.1007/s40062-020-00272-2
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/arXiv:1911.09990"} arXiv:1911.09990
          %p
            The formulation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstrings"} superstrings
            (and other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-WZW models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super L-∞ algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+extensions"} L-∞ extensions
            of) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+group"} super translation group
            is in
          %ul
            %li#FSS12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.5264"} arXiv:1308.5264
          %h3#in_solid_state_physics In solid state physics
          %p The low-energy physics of a Heisenberg antiferromagnetic spin chain is argued to be described by a WZW model in
          %ul
            %li
              Zheng-Xin Liu, Guang-Ming Zhang,
              %em Classification of quantum critical states of integrable antiferromagnetic spin chains and their correspondent two-dimensional topological phases
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.5421"}> arXiv:1211.5421
              )
          %p See also section 7.10 of Fradkin’s book.
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+protected+topological+order"} symmetry protected topological order
            phases of matter in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+WZW+models"} higher dimensional WZW models
            is in
          %ul
            %li#CGLW11
              Xie Chen, Zheng-Cheng Gu, Zheng-Xin Liu,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Gang+Wen"} Xiao-Gang Wen
              = succeed "," do
                %em Symmetry protected topological orders and the group cohomology of their symmetry group
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.4772"} arXiv:1106.4772
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 338
              %a{:href => "http://dao.mit.edu/~wen/pub/dDSPTsht.pdf"} pdf
          %div
            %h3#FractionalLevelWZWModelReferences On fractional-level WZW models as logarithmic CFTs
            %p
              On
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+models"} WZW models
              at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} fractional
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+%28Chern-Simons+theory%29"} level
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sunil+Mukhi"}> Sunil Mukhi
                  , Sudhakar Panda,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Fractional-level current algebras and the classification of characters
                  %strong 338
                  1 (1990) 263-282
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(90)90632-N"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(90)90632-N
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li#MooreRead91
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"}> Gregory Moore
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Read"} Nicholas Read
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Nonabelions in the fractional quantum hall effect
                  %strong 360
                  2–3 (1991) 362-396
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(91)90407-O"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(91)90407-O
                  %a{:href => "https://www.physics.rutgers.edu/~gmoore/MooreReadNonabelions.pdf"} pdf
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    (suggesting the fractional level
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 5
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 4
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = -5/4
                    as related to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laughlin+wavefunctions"} Laughlin wavefunctions
                    of
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anyons"} anyons
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hidetoshi+Awata"}> Hidetoshi Awata
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yasuhiko+Yamada"} Yasuhiko Yamada
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Fusion rules for the fractional level
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mi 𝔰𝔩
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 2
